/*
 * TB331FC (Lenovo Xiaoxin Pad 2024, khaje / SM6225-AD / Snapdragon 685)
 * Windows-on-ARM DSDT -- device specific.
 *
 * Provenance
 *   ancestor : topaz-woa  uefi/acpi/tapas-DSDT-xhci.dsl   (Redmi Note 12 4G,
 *              same SM6225-AD, booted Windows 11 ARM64 under Mu-Silicium)
 *   upstream : Qualcomm SM6225 stock DSDT (OEMID "QCOMM ", TableID "SM6225 ")
 *   base     : the table currently shipped in
 *              Silicium-ACPI/Platforms/Lenovo/tb331fcPkg/AcpiTables/DSDT.aml
 *              (3734 bytes, OEMID QCOMM/SM6225, INTL 20260930)
 *
 * Device facts cross-checked against the *board* device tree, not the SoC
 * baseline: vendor_boot dtb (SoC base, ufshc disabled) + dtbo.img entries 2
 * ("KHAJE IDP nopmi") and 18 ("Khajeg IDP"), board-id 0x10022, which
 * re-enable ufshc_mem with status="ok" and carry the Himax touch /
 * charger / keys nodes.  See REPORT.md.
 *
 * Delta against the shipped table
 *   - OEM ID "LENOVO", OEM Table ID "TB331FC" (was QCOMM / SM6225)
 *   - 15 orphan _SB Names from the deleted URS0 container removed
 *   - _DDN descriptions on UFS0 / USB0 / GPU0
 *   - UFSE switch + UFS0._STA, mirroring GPU0's GPUE pattern
 *   - UFS0 is RETAINED on purpose: Windows binds storufs.sys to
 *     ACPI\QCOM24A5.  Removing it (as the earlier "purified" DSL did) leaves
 *     Windows with no block storage at all.
 *
 * Build: iasl DSDT.dsl     (Intel iasl 20230628, expect 0 Errors 0 Warnings)
 */

